UPDATE companies SET description='Wisconsin Log Furniture and Railings operates from Wausaukee, Wisconsin. The business traces its roots to 2014 when the founder built a log chaise lounge chair, sparking a passion for rustic woodworking. The current name was adopted in 2019, and the company remains a family-owned operation.

The shop produces custom rustic furniture and log railings, all handmade from locally sourced white cedar, aspen, hickory, and barnwood. Offerings include indoor and outdoor furniture collections, cedar log railings with options such as metal spindles, rustic metal panels, and stainless-steel cable, as well as white cedar shutters. Each piece is built to order in a Northeast Wisconsin workshop, with no two items identical due to the natural character of the logs.

Customers span the United States, including homeowners furnishing cabins and primary residences, hospitality operators outfitting Airbnb and vacation rental properties, and commercial clients seeking rustic fixtures for lodges and retail spaces. The Durango Bedroom Collection, blending aspen and barnwood, is marketed directly to these segments.

The company emphasizes sustainably harvested white cedar obtained from local foresters within hours of the shop. A craftsmanship guarantee promises continued collaboration until the client is satisfied, reflecting the founder''s original goal of creating unique, durable pieces that last for years.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture manufacturing", "Custom log railing fabrication", "Handcrafted woodworking", "Sustainable wood sourcing", "Design consultation", "White cedar shutter production"], "industries": ["Residential (cabins, homes)", "Hospitality (Airbnb, vacation rentals)", "Commercial property"], "materials": ["White Cedar", "Cedar", "Aspen", "Hickory", "Barnwood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sustainably harvested white cedar sourced from local foresters within hours of the shop", "Every piece fully custom and one-of-a-kind due to natural log variation", "Craftsmanship guarantee: work continues until the customer is completely satisfied", "Handmade construction with attention to detail on each item", "Family-owned and operated since 2014"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 with first log chaise lounge chair -> /about-us", "Business name adopted 2019 -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /, /about-us", "Location: Wausaukee, Wisconsin (Northeast Wisconsin) -> db, /about-us", "Products: custom rustic furniture, log railings, shutters, Durango Bedroom Collection -> /, /about-us", "Materials: white cedar, aspen, hickory, barnwood -> /, /about-us", "Sustainably harvested white cedar from local foresters -> /about-us", "Fully custom, one-of-a-kind pieces -> /about-us", "Craftsmanship guarantee -> /, /about-us", "Serves residential, hospitality (Airbnb), commercial -> /", "Handmade construction -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a small, family run business that builds and supplies custom rustic furniture and log railings", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wisconsin-log-furniture-and-railings' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wisconsin Plastics Inc (WPI) is headquartered in Green Bay, Wisconsin. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure in the provided materials. It describes itself as an "idea company" that turns concepts into custom-manufactured products through collaboration with customers and a network of capabilities.

WPI operates as a contract manufacturer specializing in scientific molding, electromechanical assembly, and integrated product design. Its service portfolio spans project management, product design, scientific molding, electromechanical assemblies, integrated technology, distribution and fulfillment, and contract manufacturing. The company also designs and fabricates automated assembly fixtures, performs clean-room and electronic assembly, and offers UL-approved assembly, soldering, and testing. It sources and warehouses externally manufactured components and provides direct shipping via FedEx, UPS, LTL, and full-load carriers with full EDI capabilities.

The company serves defense and aerospace, medical, automotive, retail, and industrial sectors. It highlights cutting-edge design and quality procedures for demanding defense and aerospace environments, and produces sterile, biocompatible components for medical devices.

WPI emphasizes a value-based approach that aims to deliver better communication, lower costs, and shorter lead times by taking projects from consumer research through production implementation. It maintains a sustainability program that includes using regrind, recycling, energy-efficient hybrid molding machines, closed-loop water systems, and membership in the EPA''s Green Supplier Network.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Scientific molding", "Electromechanical assembly", "Contract manufacturing", "Project management", "Product design", "Integrated technology", "Distribution and fulfillment", "Automated assembly fixture design and fabrication", "Clean room assembly", "Electronic assembly", "Sourcing and warehousing of externally manufactured components", "UL-approved assembly, soldering, and testing", "Direct package shipping (FedEx, UPS, LTL, full-load)", "EDI capabilities"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Medical", "Automotive", "Retail", "Industrial"], "materials": ["ABS", "Polycarbonate", "Nylon", "Polyethylene"], "equipment": ["Electric and hybrid electric molding machines", "Closed-loop water systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Standard cycles range from a few weeks to a few months", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end service from consumer research through production implementation", "ISO-certified quality management with automated inspection", "Energy-efficient electric and hybrid molding machines with closed-loop water systems", "Green Supplier Network member with waste reduction and recycling programs", "Direct shipping via FedEx, UPS, LTL, and full-load with full EDI capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Green Bay, Wisconsin -> db", "Contract manufacturer specializing in scientific molding, electromechanical assembly, product design -> /, /capabilities", "Capabilities: scientific molding, electromechanical assemblies, contract manufacturing, project management, product design, integrated technology, distribution & fulfillment -> /, /capabilities", "Automated assembly fixture design and fabrication -> /capabilities, /about", "Clean room assembly and electronic assembly -> /about (products)", "UL-approved assembly, soldering, and testing -> /about (products)", "Sourcing and warehousing of externally manufactured components -> /about (products)", "Direct package shipment via FedEx, UPS, LTL, full-load -> /capabilities", "Full EDI capabilities -> /capabilities", "Industries served: defense, aerospace, medical, automotive, retail, industrial -> /, /about", "Materials: ABS, polycarbonate, nylon, polyethylene -> /about", "ISO-certified quality management systems -> /about", "Automated inspection processes -> /about", "Energy-efficient electric and hybrid electric molding machines -> /about", "Closed-loop water systems -> /about", "Green Supplier Network member -> /about", "Waste reduction using regrind and recycling -> /about", "Lead time: standard cycles range from a few weeks to a few months -> /about", "Sustainability: biodegradable plastics, recycled materials -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract manufacturing in plastics involves design, prototyping, production, and assembly of plastic components for various industries. WPI specializes in custom solutions.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wisconsin-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wits End Fabrication operates from Halethorpe, Maryland, serving the Baltimore–Washington area. The shop is led by Kenny Belt and combines automotive repair with custom metal fabrication under one roof.

The shop provides general auto repair and maintenance, differential overhauls, custom exhaust and intercooler plumbing, rust and frame repair, performance and off-road upgrades, welding repairs and fabrication, and CNC plasma cutting for commercial and specialty projects. Work ranges from daily-driver maintenance to one-off chassis fabrication, using mild steel, 304 stainless, aluminum, and titanium.

Customers include individual vehicle owners, off-road enthusiasts, and commercial equipment operators. Differential work is supported through East Coast Gear Supply and Yukon Gear & Axle. The shop also takes on CNC and commercial fabrication for businesses and specialty projects.

The company emphasizes that "custom does not come in a box," positioning itself as problem solvers who blend repair knowledge with fabrication skills. A social-media post notes that quality is the number-one priority, citing a remade radiator shroud as an example.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["General auto repair & maintenance", "Diagnostics", "Brake service", "Steering & suspension repair", "Differential overhaul & gearing", "Ring-and-pinion service", "Limited-slip & locker upgrades", "Custom exhaust fabrication", "Intercooler plumbing", "Rust & frame repair", "Performance & off-road upgrades", "Engine-swap support", "Suspension upgrades", "Bumper fabrication", "Welding repairs & fabrication", "Custom bracket, rack & chassis fabrication", "CNC plasma cutting", "Custom component fabrication for equipment", "Commercial fabrication"], "industries": ["Automotive repair", "Custom automotive fabrication", "Off-road & performance vehicles", "Commercial & industrial equipment fabrication"], "materials": ["Mild steel", "304 stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Titanium"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma cutter", "Baileigh fabrication equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Repair and fabrication under one roof", "Custom exhaust and intercooler plumbing built around vehicle routing", "Differential overhauls with East Coast Gear Supply and Yukon Gear & Axle support", "CNC plasma cutting for commercial and specialty projects", "Welding in mild steel, 304 stainless, aluminum, and titanium"], "facts_used": ["Location: Halethorpe, Maryland -> /", "Address: 1907 Lansdowne Road, Halethorpe, MD 21227 -> /", "Founder/leader: Kenny Belt -> /about", "Services: General auto repair & maintenance, differential overhauls, custom exhausts, intercooler plumbing, rust & frame repair, performance & off-road, welding, CNC plasma cutting -> /services", "Materials: Mild steel, 304 stainless, aluminum, titanium -> /services", "Differential co