UPDATE companies SET description='Wolfspeed operates a silicon carbide semiconductor fabrication facility in Fayetteville, Arkansas. The company is the world''s only pure-play, vertically integrated silicon carbide manufacturer, producing both substrates and power devices under one roof.

The Fayetteville site manufactures silicon carbide substrates, power modules, discrete power devices (including MOSFETs and Schottky diodes), and power die products. Wolfspeed has recently expanded to 200 mm wafer processing, introducing premium n-type SiC substrates that improve yield per wafer and per lot. The company provides design support tools, reference designs, evaluation kits, and gate driver boards to accelerate customer development. Its "silicon carbide corridor" enables end-to-end fabrication from substrate to finished device at massive scale.

Concrete examples include a partnership with Stercom to scale grid-compatible V2X technology for heavy-duty EVs, a long-term wafer supply agreement with Infineon, and collaboration with Amperesand on medium-voltage solid-state transformers for AI data centers.

Wolfspeed differentiates itself through its pioneering role in silicon carbide, vertical integration from substrate to system, and a focus on enabling electrification and sustainability. The company emphasizes safety, integrity, ingenuity, and ownership as core values guiding its operations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Silicon carbide substrate manufacturing", "Power device fabrication (MOSFETs, Schottky diodes)", "Power module assembly", "Power die production", "200 mm wafer processing", "Design support tools and reference designs", "Evaluation kits and gate driver boards", "Automotive qualification (AEC-Q101) and PPAP", "Solid-state transformer development (partnered)"], "industries": ["Automotive (electric vehicles)", "Renewable energy", "Industrial motor drives", "Aerospace", "Data centers (AI hyperscale)", "Commercial and off-highway EVs", "Grid infrastructure (solid-state transformers)", "Racing"], "materials": ["Silicon carbide (SiC)", "200 mm n-type SiC substrates", "SiC MOSFETs", "SiC Schottky diodes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s only pure-play, vertically integrated silicon carbide company", "Largest pure-play provider of SiC substrates globally", "First U.S.-based end-to-end silicon carbide corridor (substrate to power device)", "200 mm n-type SiC substrates with multi-metric quality improvement"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Fayetteville, Arkansas -> db", "World''s only pure-play, vertically integrated silicon carbide company -> /", "Largest pure-play provider of SiC substrates in the world -> /about", "Produces silicon carbide substrates, power modules, discrete power devices, power die products -> /about", "200 mm n-type SiC substrates with multi-metric quality leap -> /", "Design support tools, reference designs, evaluation kits, gate driver boards -> /about", "First U.S.-based silicon carbide corridor with end-to-end substrate and power device fabrication -> /", "Serves automotive (AEC-Q101 qualified), renewable energy, industrial, aerospace, data centers, commercial EVs -> /, /about, industries_served", "Partnership with Stercom for grid-compatible V2X technology -> /", "Long-term wafer supply agreement with Infineon -> /", "Collaboration with Amperesand on medium-voltage solid-state transformers -> /", "Core values: Safety, Integrity & Respect; Ingenuity & Passion; Ownership & Accountability -> /about", "Automotive qualified (AEC-Q101) and PPAP capable -> industries_served", "Wolfspeed, Inc. fiscal earnings call -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "world''s only pure-play, vertically integrated silicon carbide company", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wolfspeed-fayetteville' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wood Machinery Systems (WMS) is headquartered in Minnetonka, Minnesota, where Jim Besonen founded the company in 1995 to supply woodworking and furniture manufacturers with high‑tech equipment and a lifetime of customer support. The business remains family‑owned and locally operated.

WMS distributes new and used woodworking machinery from a range of global brands, covering categories such as boring machines, dovetailers, moulders, saws, sanders, dust collectors, and router bits. The company also stocks parts and tooling for wood, aluminum, composites, and plastics. Beyond equipment sales, WMS provides installation, hands‑on training, repair, warranty service, technical maintenance, consulting, and financing through a partnership with Stearns Bank.

The customer base spans home hobbyists, specialty boutiques, and large‑scale manufacturers producing windows, doors, cabinets, clocks, and other wood products. WMS serves clients throughout the Midwest and beyond, positioning itself as a supply‑chain link for businesses of all sizes.

