UPDATE companies SET description='Wood-Mizer Manufacturing is based in Batesville, Indiana. Founded in 1982, the company began as a garage startup and has grown into a global family business, though ownership details are not explicitly stated.

The company designs, engineers, and manufactures portable sawmills, bandsaw blades, and a range of wood-processing equipment including pallet equipment, log splitters, and custom industrial sawmilling systems. Its product line spans more than 20 sawmill models priced from $2,995, serving hobbyists, DIY woodworkers, and high-volume professional operations. Blades are produced in the United States and built to cut extreme hardwoods and frozen logs.

Wood-Mizer serves customers across hobby sawmilling, commercial lumber production, pallet manufacturing, and specialty timber markets. Its equipment has been used by distillers such as Hollerhorn Distilling, builders like Charles Singleton who milled tornado-damaged timber for a dovetail cabin, guitar-makers sourcing rare Australian species through David Linton, and historic restoration projects including a 1779 New England barn. The company also showcases its sawmills at more than 125 trade shows annually.

Wood-Mizer emphasizes American manufacturing of its blades and custom-engineered industrial solutions designed to maximize yield and reduce operational costs. The company’s stated differentiation rests on providing portable sawmills for every stage of operation, from entry-level to high-production, backed by a full line of accessories and replacement parts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Portable sawmill manufacturing", "Bandsaw blade manufacturing", "Custom industrial sawmilling system design", "Pallet equipment manufacturing", "Log splitter manufacturing", "Sawmill accessory production", "Power feed and trailer fabrication", "Replacement parts supply"], "industries": ["Hobby woodworking", "Commercial sawmilling", "Lumber production", "Pallet manufacturing", "Log processing", "Specialty timber milling", "Historic restoration", "Musical instrument wood supply", "Distilling"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Portable sawmills", "Bandsaw blades", "Power feeds", "Trailers", "Pallet equipment", "Log splitters", "Custom industrial sawmilling systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Bandsaw blades engineered and manufactured in the USA", "Custom industrial sawmilling solutions tailored to maximize yield and reduce costs", "Portable sawmills for hobby to high-volume production", "Free shipping on select sawmill blades, parts, and accessories", "Presence at 125+ trade shows annually"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Batesville, Indiana -> db", "Founded in 1982 -> description (db)", "Manufactures portable sawmills, bandsaw blades, accessories, pallet equipment, log splitters -> page ''/''", "Blades engineered and manufactured in USA -> page ''/''", "Custom industrial sawmilling solutions -> page ''/''", "20+ sawmill models from $2,995 -> page ''/''", "Serves hobbyists, DIY, professional sawyers -> page ''/''", "Customer examples: Hollerhorn Distilling, Charles Singleton, David Linton, Alan Spooner, Kenney Batch