UPDATE companies SET description='Woodland was founded in 1996 by Lynn and Pat Harker in Idaho Falls, Idaho. Pat Harker, drawing on experience from her design firm Harker Design, envisioned a resource that would serve interior designers with high-quality products, service excellence, delivery in under 12 weeks, and fair pricing.

Today Woodland produces cabinetry, lighting, and upholstery as a whole-home solution for designers. The operation emphasizes custom designs and custom finishes, relying on craft and artistry rather than full automation. The facility earned the Shingo Prize in 2000 for excellence in lean manufacturing, reflecting a commitment to continuous improvement on the shop floor.

The primary customers are interior design professionals and design firms seeking tailored residential furnishings. Designers specify Woodland pieces for custom residential projects, relying on the company’s ability to translate design intent into finished cabinetry, lighting fixtures, and upholstered goods.

Woodland differentiates itself through its dedication to handcrafted custom work, a stated delivery target of under 12 weeks, and a pricing philosophy described as fair.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry", "Custom lighting", "Custom upholstery", "Custom finishes", "Lean manufacturing", "Interior design collaboration"], "industries": ["Interior design", "Residential furniture", "Home furnishings"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Under 12 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Delivery in under 12 weeks", "Custom designs and custom finishes", "Shingo Prize for lean manufacturing (2000)", "Fair pricing", "Service excellence"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 by Lynn and Pat Harker in Idaho Falls, Idaho -> /about", "Awarded Shingo Prize in 2000 for lean manufacturing -> /about", "Produces cabinetry, lighting, and upholstery as whole-home solution -> /about", "Focus on custom designs and custom finishes -> /about", "Delivery target under 12 weeks -> /about", "Serves interior design community -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Woodland has continued to grow through the addition of Cabinetry, Lighting, and Upholstery to create a whole home solution for designers.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='woodland' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Woodland Manufacturing operates from Meridian, Idaho, where it was founded in 2003 as a limited liability company. The business began in a garage with computer-guided saws nicknamed "The Beast," cutting wooden letters for custom signage.

Today the shop produces custom sign letters, plaques, and event displays using wood, metal (aluminum, bronze, steel, brass, copper), plastic (acrylic, foam, formed and injection-molded), and vinyl. In-house capabilities include CNC routing, laser cutting, water jet cutting, vinyl cutting, and media production. The company describes its workshop as stocked and its capabilities as virtually limitless, though it does not disclose facility size, headcount, or annual volumes.

Customers range from businesses, churches, and government offices to industrial shops and event organizers. The company notes that its clients often have a DIY attitude and confidence in designing and installing their own signage, and it supports them with installation guides and finishing tutorials.

