UPDATE companies SET description='ZM Sheet Metal was founded in 1967 when Pittsburgh sheet metal worker Joe Zivic relocated to Virginia and started the business with a partner. The company has remained family-owned ever since, with Zivic''s son Scott taking over operations in the late 1980s and the next generation now working in the business. Headquartered in Winchester, Virginia, the firm operates a 100,000-square-foot manufacturing plant there and a second facility in Chantilly.

The company specializes in HVAC ductwork and sheet metal fabrication, working primarily with galvanized steel, black iron, stainless steel, and aluminum. With a workforce of 100 employees who collectively hold over 1,000 years of company experience, ZM Sheet Metal produces components for distribution across nine states — Maryland, Delaware, Pennsylvania, New York, New Jersey, Connecticut, New Hampshire, and the District of Columbia. All manufacturing takes place at the two Virginia locations.

ZM Sheet Metal serves HVAC manufacturers and commercial ductwork contractors through a network of exclusive distributors, each granted a protected geographic territory. Its customer base spans the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic regions, with distributors acting as the primary channel to mechanical contractors and building projects.

