UPDATE companies SET description='603 Metals operates from a shop at 724 E. Industrial Park Drive in Manchester, New Hampshire. The business was founded in January 2020 by Brian McKenna, who comes from a multi‑generational line of metalworkers tracing back to bronze workers in Ireland and a family shop in southern New Hampshire. After apprenticing under his uncle Charles Macdonald — an internationally recognized master in marine metal fabrication at CJM Custom Shop in Fort Lauderdale — McKenna managed a large production dock and gangway shop in Pompano Beach before returning to his roots to open 603 Metals.

The company provides custom metal fabrication, architectural metalwork, railings and stairs, metal art, dock and gangway solutions, and marine fabrication. Core processes include plasma, laser, and water‑jet cutting; machining; polishing; welding; and a full range of finishing services such as galvanizing, electrostatic painting, powder coating, sand blasting, patina, brushed, polished, anodized, and plated finishes. The shop also handles design, project management, and installation, working from a single facility in Manchester.

