UPDATE companies SET description='A&M Plastics operates from South Houston, Texas, where Arthur and Kathy Mason founded the company in 1988. The couple met while working in the plastics industry in the Midwest, then moved to Texas to build their own business. They started with two injection molding machines that Arthur salvaged from a field and restored himself, laying the groundwork for what remains a family-owned operation today.

The shop runs ten injection molding presses and two extrusion lines, supported by machining, assembly, sonic welding, hot stamping, and other secondary operations. Over more than 35 years the company has brought hundreds of products to market and shipped millions of parts.

Customers span automotive, medical, oil and gas, construction, and consumer-products sectors. Named accounts include Igloo, Parker Hannifin, Emerson, Safety Maker, and projects supporting NASA; a testimonial from Liquid Health Labs highlights quick setup and reliable delivery.

