UPDATE companies SET description='ABB is headquartered in Cary, North Carolina. The company was founded in 1988.

ABB manufactures switchgear, circuit breakers, transformers, and electric motors, and provides electrification, automation, robotics, and digital solutions. Its portfolio includes the SACE Emax 3 air circuit breaker, the GoFa collaborative robot with ultra-accuracy, Azipod electric propulsion systems, and the ABB Ability Digital Powertrain for remote asset monitoring. The company operates across electrification, automation, motion, robotics, and power conversion, delivering products ranging from medium-voltage switchgear to industrial IoT and AI suites.

Customers span buildings and construction, data centers, food and beverage, marine shipping, oil and gas, and power generation utilities. ABB notes that one in four data centers worldwide run on its technology, and its solutions are used to decarbonize shipping and optimize energy infrastructure. Its automation business offers industry-specific integrated automation, control technologies, software, and advanced services.

ABB positions itself as a global technology leader in electrification and automation, aiming to help industries become more productive, efficient, and sustainable so they can ''outrun'' competitors. The company emphasizes connecting engineering and digitalization expertise to accelerate decarbonization and increase energy efficiency.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Switchgear manufacturing", "Circuit breaker manufacturing", "Transformer manufacturing", "Electric motor manufacturing", "Electrification solutions", "Process and hybrid industry automation", "Industrial robotics (industrial and collaborative robots)", "Autonomous mobile robots (AMRs)", "Power conversion and control", "Renewable power integration", "Industrial IoT and AI analytics (ABB Genix)", "Digital powertrain monitoring (ABB Ability)", "Electric propulsion systems (Azipod)", "Measurement and analytics", "Marine automation solutions"], "industries": ["Buildings and construction", "Data centers", "Food and beverage", "Marine shipping", "Oil and gas", "Power generation utilities", "Process industries", "Hybrid industries"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SACE Emax 3 air circuit breaker", "ABB Genix Industrial IoT and AI Suite", "GoFa collaborative robot", "Azipod electric propulsion system", "ABB Ability Digital Powertrain"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One in four data centers run on ABB technology", "GoFa cobot offers 10 times greater path accuracy than other cobots", "Azipod electric propulsion revolutionized marine transport with unparalleled efficiency", "SACE Emax 3 air circuit breaker makes electrical distribution more adaptive and secure", "ABB Ability Digital Powertrain enables remote monitoring of powertrain health and energy efficiency"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Cary, North Carolina -> db", "Founded in 1988 -> db", "Manufactures switchgear, circuit breakers, transformers, electric motors -> db", "Offers electrification, automation, robotics, digital solutions -> homepage", "SACE Emax 3 air circuit breaker -> homepage", "GoFa cobot with ultra accuracy -> homepage", "Azipod electric propulsion -> homepage", "ABB Ability Digital Powertrain -> homepage", "One in four data centers run on ABB technology -> homepage", "Serves buildings, data centers, food and beverage, marine, oil and gas, utilities -> homepage", "Positions as global technology leader in electrification and automation -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Global manufacturer of switchgear, circuit breakers, transformers, and electric motors.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='abb' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ABCO Automation Inc. was founded in 1977 by Graham Ricks in Browns Summit, North Carolina. The company began by providing electrical control systems and custom packaging equipment to Coca-Cola, and early innovations in labeling and filling led to significant growth throughout the 1980s. In the mid-1990s, ABCO transitioned to an employee-owned ESOP structure, a model the leadership credits for a highly motivated workforce.

Today, ABCO operates two facilities in Browns Summit: a Design Build Complex and a Contract Manufacturing & Assembly Center. The company delivers custom automation solutions through four core service lines: Design Build, Build to Print, Contract Manufacturing, and Robot Automation. Its engineering and manufacturing capabilities span mechanical and electrical design, fabrication, welding, assembly, kitting, inspection, laser marking, machining, machine tending, dispensing, and material handling integration. The firm serves clients ranging from Fortune 500 corporations to start-ups.

ABCO''s industry focus includes food and beverage, logistics, life sciences, AgriTech, and healthcare. Long-standing relationships with major food and beverage brands such as Coca-Cola illustrate its experience with filling systems, packaging, and palletizing.

The company emphasizes a single-source, turnkey approach backed by decades of mechanical and electrical engineering expertise. Its stated mission is to provide a single source for innovative automation services and manufacturing support that contribute to client success, guided by core values that prioritize client needs, integrity, excellence, and teamwork.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design Build", "Build to Print", "Contract Manufacturing", "Robot Automation", "Palletizing", "Case Erecting", "Case Packing", "Conveyor Systems", "DePalletizing", "Welding", "Assembly", "Kitting", "Bin Picking", "Cutting", "Inspection", "Laser Marking", "Grinding", "Milling / Routing", "Machine Tending", "BIB Liquid Dispensing", "Dispensing", "FIPG (Form-in-Place Gasket)", "Mechanical Design", "Electrical Design", "Fabrication"], "industries": ["Food & Beverage", "Logistics", "Life Sciences", "AgriTech", "Healthcare", "General Industry"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned ESOP since the mid-1990s", "Single-source turnkey solutions covering design, build, contract manufacturing, and robot automation", "Decades of mechanical and electrical engineering expertise", "Dedicated project management with field support and comprehensive documentation", "Proven track record with Fortune 500 companies and start-ups"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1977 by Graham Ricks -> /about", "Employee-owned ESOP since mid-1990s -> /about", "Headquarters in Browns Summit, NC -> /about", "Two facilities: Design Build Complex and Contract Manufacturing & Assembly Center -> /about", "Services: Design Build, Build to Print, Contract Manufacturing, Robot Automation -> /about, /", "Industries: Food & Beverage, Logistics, Life Sciences, AgriTech, Healthcare -> /about, /", "Automation solutions: Palletizing, Case Erector, Case Packer, Conveyors, DePalletizing, Welding, Assembly, Kitting, Bin Picking, Cutting, Inspection, Laser Marking, Grinding, Mill/Routing, Machine Tending, BIB Liquid, Dispensing, FIPG -> /", "Mission and core values -> /about", "History with Coca-Cola -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Manufacturing: From assembly and building, to welding and quality control, ABCO offers all the manufacturing services you need to reduce costs and labor.", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='abco-automation-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ABX Innovative Packaging Solutions is a flexible packaging manufacturer headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina, with manufacturing facilities across the United States including sites in Rhinelander, Wisconsin; Columbus, Georgia; Homer, Louisiana; Macedon, New York; Milwaukee and Pewaukee, Wisconsin; and Schaumburg, Illinois. The company operates nine facilities and employs approximately nine hundred people.

The company produces flexible packaging through a fully integrated process that spans film extrusion, converting, pouching, bagging, printing, and laminating. Its extrusion lines produce coextruded cast and blown films up to 11 layers with thickness capabilities from 1 to 13 mil, using specialty resin blends such as nylon, polypropylene, EVOH, ionomers, and metallocene. Converting operations include stand‑up pouches, rollstock, and a fleet of more than 45 bag machines, while printing is handled on wide‑web W&H flexographic presses with AVT registration. In‑house design consulting, structural testing, and analytical labs support development from concept to commercialization.

ABX serves customers in consumer, healthcare, industrial, and specialty markets, with specific applications in food, personal care, and medical packaging. Its client base includes brands seeking high‑barrier, breathable, or sustainable film structures for products ranging from individual portions to large‑format industrial bags.

The company emphasizes a one‑stop‑shop model from resin to finished package, backed by third‑party quality audits and certifications. It highlights its status as the first plant to earn FTA FIRST certification for wide‑web printers, along with ISO 9001:2015, AIB Superior Rating, HACCP procedures, and FDA‑approved materials as differentiators that support safety, consistency, and regulatory compliance.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AIB Superior Rating','HACCP Manufacturing Procedures','FDA Approved Materials','CFIA','FTA FIRST certification (wide‑web printing)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Coextruded cast film extrusion (up to 11 layers)", "Blown film extrusion", "High\u2011barrier, standard\u2011barrier, and breathable film structures", "Wide\u2011web extrusion (1\u201313 mil thickness)", "Specialty resin blending (nylon, PP, EVOH, ionomers, metallocene)", "Stand\u2011up pouch and rollstock converting", "Flexographic printing (10\u2011color, wide\u2011web, AVT registration)", "Custom laminating (30\u2013120\" width, foil, paper, woven/non\u2011woven substrates)", "Slitting (2\u2013120\" width)", "Bag making (perforations, zippers, gussets, hermetic seals, handles, headers)", "Package design consulting (die lines, prepress, color management)", "Analytical testing (ASTM methods, OTR/WVTR, bond/burst, COF, haze, tensile, hot tack)"], "industries": ["Consumer packaging", "Healthcare packaging", "Industrial packaging", "Specialty packaging", "Food packaging", "Personal care packaging"], "materials": ["Nylon", "Polypropylene (PP)", "EVOH", "Ionomers (Surlyn\u00ae)", "Metallocene", "Aluminum foil (0.25\u20131 mil)", "Lightweight papers to heavy linerboards", "Woven and non\u2011woven fabrics"], "equipment": ["W&H flexographic printing presses", "AVT registration system", "45+ bag making machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One\u2011stop\u2011shop from resin to final product", "First plant to earn FTA FIRST certification for wide\u2011web printers", "45+ bag machines in\u2011house", "ISO 9001:2015, AIB Superior Rating, HACCP procedures", "In\u2011house design consulting and structural testing labs"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Charlotte, NC -> /about", "Nine facilities, nine hundred employees -> /about", "Manufacturing sites in Rhinelander WI, Columbus GA, Homer LA, Macedon NY, Milwaukee WI, Pewaukee WI, Schaumburg IL -> /", "Film extrusion up to 11 layers, 1\u201313 mil thickness -> /capabilities", "Specialty resin blends: nylon, PP, EVOH, ionomers, metallocene -> /capabilities", "Stand\u2011up pouches, rollstock, 45+ bag machines -> /capabilities", "10\u2011color wide\u2011web flexographic printing on W&H presses with AVT registration -> /capabilities", "First plant to earn FTA FIRST certification for wide\u2011web printers -> /capabilities", "Custom laminating widths 30\u2013120\", slitting 2\u2013120\" -> /capabilities", "In\u2011house design consulting, prepress, color management -> /capabilities", "Testing lab: ASTM methods, OTR/WVTR, bond/burst, COF, haze, tensile, hot tack -> /capabilities", "ISO 9001:2015 certified, AIB Superior Rating, HACCP, FDA approved materials, CFIA -> /capabilities", "Serves consumer, healthcare, industrial, specialty, food, personal care markets -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "ABX is a flexible packaging manufacturer with nine facilities and nine hundred employees.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "900", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='abx-innovative-packaging-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ACP Sheet Metal Co. Inc. operates from Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, where it was founded in 1977 by Harold Dills. The company serves the western two-thirds of the state from its facility on North Garnett Drive.

The firm fabricates and installs HVAC duct systems, including rectangular, square, round, and oval spiral ductwork, along with associated equipment and accessories. Its drafting department produces 2D and 3D shop drawings using AutoDesk, Trimble, NavisWorks, and Revit, enabling Building Information Modeling coordination to detect conflicts before installation. An industrial group designs, fabricates, and installs handrails, guardrails, stairs, platforms, catwalks, and conveyor systems, working with stainless steel, aluminum, black iron (both cold-rolled and hot-rolled), and galvanized steel. The company also provides estimating, project management, and full installation services.

ACP serves healthcare, education, institutional, military, and private-sector clients. Its industrial work spans pet care and pet food (over 40 years), food and beverage, oil and gas, mining, manufacturing, office and professional buildings, restaurants, hospitality, and the cannabis/CBD industry.

