UPDATE companies SET description='ADAR Technologies is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona. The company was formed in 2025 by CEO Dan Kelly, COO Doug Farrington, and Technology Advisor Arie Bos, following three years of development that began in 2022 with a prototype in the Netherlands. The founders set out to solve the problem of wet organic materials — manure, sludge, surplus produce — that were too costly to dry conventionally and too valuable to discard.

ADAR’s core technology, called ADS, dries, pulverizes, and sanitizes waste in a single pass without fossil fuels, added heat, or harmful chemicals. The process yields a dry, odorless, pathogen-free powder that retains the full nutritional profile of the source material. The company commercializes this output in two ways: it sells spec‑consistent powder ingredients — high‑protein supplements from seaweed and seafood waste, zeolite powder, and nutrient‑rich fertilizer from manure — directly to formulators and blenders in the feed, pet food, fertilizer, fuel, and mineral markets; and through ADAR Environmental Services it assumes waste streams from generators at roughly half their current disposal cost, turning liability into feedstock.

Primary customers include animal‑nutrition formulators, pet‑food manufacturers, fertilizer blenders, and industrial mineral processors. A global agricultural company has already endorsed the technology for converting sargassum seaweed and seafood waste into high‑protein livestock feed. Municipal sewage, agricultural by‑products, and wood‑chip waste are also cited as feedstocks.

The company’s differentiation rests on three claims: zero‑emission processing, 100 % nutrient retention, and a business model that cuts waste‑disposal costs by 50 % while creating salable ingredients. The founders state that no thermal process has previously achieved a shelf‑stable, pathogen‑free powder with complete nutrient integrity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["ADS waste drying, pulverizing, and sanitizing", "Organic waste upcycling to high-protein powder", "Mineral waste upcycling to zeolite powder", "Manure conversion to fertilizer powder", "Seaweed (sargassum) conversion to protein supplement", "Seafood waste conversion to protein supplement", "Wood chip moisture reduction and mold eradication", "Waste stream management at reduced disposal cost"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Livestock feed", "Pet food", "Fertilizer", "Fuel", "Mineral processing", "Green energy"], "materials": ["Manure", "Seaweed (Sargassum)", "Zeolite", "Wood chips", "Wet bark", "Sawdust", "Seafood waste", "Municipal sewage", "Agricultural byproducts", "Surplus produce", "Sludge"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dries, pulverizes, and sanitizes waste without fossil fuels, added heat, or chemicals", "Zero\u2011emission process with 100% nutrient retention", "Converts waste into salable powder ingredients at 50% of current disposal cost", "Single\u2011step resource recovery that eliminates odors and pathogens"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Founded 2025 by Dan Kelly, Doug Farrington, Arie Bos -> /about", "Technology ADS dries, pulverizes, sanitizes without fossil fuels/heat/chemicals -> /", "Prototype built in Netherlands 2024, tested 70+ materials -> /about", "Sells powder ingredients directly to formulators/blenders -> /about", "ADAR Environmental Services takes waste streams at 50% disposal cost -> /about", "Converts seaweed, seafood waste to high-protein supplement for agriculture/livestock -> /", "Converts manure to nutrient-rich fertilizer -> /", "Produces zeolite powder for commercial applications -> /", "Processes wood chips, wet bark, sawdust reducing moisture and mold -> /", "Industries: feed, pet food, fertilizer, fuel, mineral markets -> /about", "Customer example: global agricultural company -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, ADAR is a premium ingredients company. We upcycle the world\u2019s overlooked organic and mineral streams into the most nutrient-complete powder ingredients ever brought to market \u2014 and we sell them directly to the formulators and blenders who know the difference.", "founded_year": "2025", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='adar-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
